#![enable(implicit_some)]
// Unit, structure and mission-object definitions (WP3.1): one record per role of
// content/units.md, with its design-target stats. Read by sf_data::units, which
// checks every reference; docs/rules/units.md describes each field.
//
// ORDER IS THE KIND NUMBER. The simulation's `Kind` is the position of a record
// in this list, so append new roles at the end and never reorder or remove one
// that a scenario or a save may use. Adding a role is only a new record here
// (and weapons in weapon_defs.ron, if it needs new ones): no Rust change.
//
// Units of measure: distances, sizes and sight in cells (1 cell = 4 m, B12);
// speed in cells per game second (20 ticks); build_seconds in game seconds;
// turn_rate in facing steps (256 per full turn) per tick; cost in credits;
// power in power units (+ produces, - uses); hp abstract.
//
// What content/units.md states is used as is: roles, cost, power, hp, speed,
// weapon ranges, capacities and radii, and the faction that gets the role in
// its tech tree. Everything else is a placeholder, marked with a
// `placeholder:` comment on the record: build_seconds, turn_rate, size, sight,
// armor type, the footprints of mission structures and the model/icon choices
// (the testpack_v1 models stand in until real art, WP11.6; roles without a
// model use a primitive shape).
(
    units: [
